WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.270
Avengers: Endgame resolved lots of questions
that went unanswered after Avengers: Infinity

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.080
War... but it didn't fully discuss the deaths
of all of the characters who died pre-Snap,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.420
namely Vision.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.960
Speaking during a recent Q&amp;A event, director
Joe Russo finally addressed Vision's fate.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.120
Consider yourself warned: Lots of spoilers
ahead!

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.640
So, who didn't survive Infinity War?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.439
Loki died early on, after Thanos strangled
him.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.920
Later, Thanos sacrificed Gamora in order to
obtain the Soul Stone.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.840
But thanks to all the time-travel woven throughout
the story, both characters eventually appear

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.850
in Endgame.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.660
However, Vision doesn't.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.980
This left viewers wondering if the android
would ever be returning, or if he's truly

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.200
gone for good.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.680
Speaking at the Q&amp;A event An Evening with
Joe Russo, the filmmaker was more than happy

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.140
to discuss Vision's fate…

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.820
But you might be less than thrilled to hear
what he has to say.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.560
The bad news: Vision was definitely killed
in Infinity War when Thanos yanked the Mind

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.000
Stone out of his forehead.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.660
Judging by a comment from Russo, that plot
point won't be undone anytime soon:

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.980
"Vision?

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.660
He's dead as far as I know."

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.740
Co-director Anthony Russo agreed with audiences
everywhere that it was heartbreaking to watch

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.800
Vision perish at the end of Infinity War,
telling Wired in 2018,

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.700
"One of the most tragic moments in the movie
and one of our favorite moments of the movie,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.540
of course, is when she has to take his life
in order to stop Thanos from getting the stone."

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.120
Then, it was doubly upsetting when the Mad
Titan reversed that effort to inflict the

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.340
damage himself.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.440
At the end of the day, Vision's death was
incredibly impactful and is probably best

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.540
left untouched.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.300
But the android's terrible fate goes one step
further; Anthony Russo noted that it was all

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.619
probably even a little bit worse than what
we saw on screen, noting that actor Paul Bettany

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.160
interprets Vision as...

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.640
"... just someone who's seeking to understand
humanity, and I think that with that final

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.700
gesture, Vision really achieved full humanity."

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.880
If Vision finally became effectively human
in that moment, the fact that Thanos used

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.500
the Time Stone to undo Scarlet Witch's efforts
and kill him himself is even more devastating.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.840
Ultimately, if the powers that be decide to
rebuild Vision, it could potentially undermine

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.260
his whole story arc, and diminish much of
the meaning behind his death.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:15.300
To complicate matters, Marvel Studios president
Kevin Feige revealed in April 2019 that the

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.400
upcoming Disney+ series WandaVision and the
future MCU movies are linked, saying,

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.810
And perhaps that goes both ways.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.970
If the MCU movies have an impact on the forthcoming
Disney+ shows just as much as the series will

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.680
impact future films, Vision's death should
influence WandaVision's story.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.300
On the flip side, if WandaVision features
a Vision who's very much alive, it might mean

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.920
he has a place in Phase 4 of the MCU.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.780
Neither Disney nor Marvel have confirmed how
that's possible in the context of the MCU,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.980
but Scarlet Witch actress Elizabeth Olsen
did tease that WandaVision would have a specific

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.980
time setting.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.800
"They showed a photo of us in the '50s?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.880
And I think that's a good teaser?"

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.160
Right now, anything can happen.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.040
Whether Marvel decides to keep him dead or
ultimately decides to revive him...

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.620
"I am on the side of life."

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.520
... we can at least be fairly confident that
we haven't seen the last of Vision.

